WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.480
On 15 September 2008, the bank
Lehman Brothers went bankrupt.

2
00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:08.530
A year earlier, savers in
Britain had rushed to pull

3
00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:11.400
their money out of a bank
called Northern Rock.

4
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.250
When a clothing chain goes bust,

5
00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:15.930
its rivals simply take its customers.

6
00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:18.530
Banks are treated very differently.

7
00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:20.970
So why do governments let most firms fail,

8
00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:24.320
but write strict rules
to stop banks failing?

9
00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:27.030
In this mission, you'll
read a bank's balance sheet,

10
00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:30.160
and see how thin its
cushion of capital can be.

11
00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:35.230
Then you'll follow the crisis
of 2007 and 2008 step by step,

12
00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:37.800
and meet the regulators built after it.

13
00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:42.610
Your mission: explain why banks are
not left to fail like other firms.
